    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0912.3717v2</id>
    <title>A New Mechanism of Quark Energy Loss</title>
    <updated>2010-02-05T14:45:40Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.3717v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0912.3717v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We show that a heavy quark moving sufficiently fast through a quark-gluon plasma may lose energy by Cherenkov-radiating mesons. We demonstrate that this takes place in all strongly coupled, large-Nc plasmas with a gravity dual. The energy loss is exactly calculable in these models despite being an O(1/Nc)-effect. We discuss phenomenological implications for heavy-ion collision experiments.</summary>
